commands to be runned in the terminal
step1: mkdir [folder_name]

step2: gedit s1.tcl 
step3: type the code inside s1.tcl then
step4: gedit s1.awk
step5: type the code inside s1.awk then
step6: after you type your code come to the terminal and run this code: sudo ns s1.tcl
step7: After you run that code youll be asked to enter the password . enter ubuntu.
step8: youll get an interface. press below where there is an empty space.
step9: press play button at the top.
step10: keep changing the Mb values like this

$ns duplex-link $n0 $n1 0.25Mb 10ms DropTail
$ns duplex-link $n1 $n2 1Mb 10ms DropTail
step11:run this 
gedit s1graph
step12: enter this values in that file
0.25 0
0.50 0
0.75 0
1.00 0
1.25 9
1.50 12
1.75 15
2.00 13
step13: then run this
xgraph -x "Bandwidth(Mbps)" -y "No of packets dropped" -t "Performance analysis" s1graph
this will give u a graph.
